# Never upload local environment files.
#
# This matters more than it looks: Next.js reads .env.local during a production
# build too, so if a local file rode along with `vercel deploy`, a development
# switch could take effect in production. NEXT_PUBLIC_DEMO_MODE is exactly such
# a switch, and it opens the member area to everyone with seeded data.
# Production gets its values from the Vercel project settings, and nowhere else.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Local tooling and notes that are not part of the deployed app.
.claude/
.agents/
.mcp.json
skills-lock.json
DESIGN.md

# Never ship the local build cache; Vercel builds fresh.
.next/
node_modules/
